  "solution": {
    "text": "Sulphur gains 8 electron in reduction and iodide ion loses 1 electron in oxidation.<br/><br/>Thus values of  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></math>  are 8, 4, 4 respectively hence the reaction is<br/><br/> <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>→</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>",
